maya: Quick check — for the chat/completions contract: what's the current decision on tool_call.args nullability vs omission? SDKs are inconsistent (TS vs Python) and we need a stable rule.
aj: My recollection: avoid nulls for fields we can omit. Historically platform sometimes omitted empty args which is annoying for TS. @kevin any final call?
kevin: For backward-compatibility we should NOT introduce nullable semantics. Rule: either include the field with an object (can be empty {}) or omit it — but prefer including {} for tool args to reduce downstream checks. Streaming deltas remain sparsely emitted (only changed keys).
rachel: +1 on documenting preference for {} for tool args. For streaming: we'll keep emitting only the changed fields; do not send explicit nulls to indicate deletion — use an explicit "op":"delete" delta if needed later. I'll add both to the schema doc.
maya: can someone paste minimal examples we can copy into SDK tests?
kevin: example message (tool call):
```json
{
  "role": "tool",
  "name": "web_search",
  "content": "results...",
  "tool_call": {
    "name": "open_web",
    "args": {}
  }
}
```
aj: streaming delta example we agreed on:
```json
{
  "delta": {
    "content": "new token content"
  }
}
```
rachel: Action items: (1) I'll open a small PR to convo-schema that states: "tool_call.args: object (prefer {}) or omitted; do not use null" and "streaming: only changed fields; no null sentinel values". (2) SDKs: maya to add lint+test to prefer {} on send.
infra-bot: Heads up — docs build scheduled in ~10m, changes will appear after CI :rocket:
maya: thanks! i'll watch the PR and update the SDK rule once merged.
